
*****************************RateLimiting************************88

1. Auth Endpoints — Brute Force Attack
Scenario: Hacker tries to guess your password
Hacker script:
POST /api/auth/login  → { email: "john@gmail.com", password: "123456" }   → 401
POST /api/auth/login  → { email: "john@gmail.com", password: "password" }  → 401
POST /api/auth/login  → { email: "john@gmail.com", password: "john1234" }  → 401
... 1000 attempts in 1 minute

Without rate limit → hacker keeps trying until they guess it
With rate limit    → blocked after 5 attempts, wait 1 minute

2. Payment Endpoints — Payment Fraud
Scenario: Someone has a stolen credit card and keeps trying
Fraudster:
POST /api/payments/create-order → amount: 999  → card declined
POST /api/payments/create-order → amount: 999  → card declined
POST /api/payments/create-order → amount: 999  → card declined
... 50 attempts in 1 minute

Without rate limit → keeps hammering your payment gateway
                     Razorpay charges you per API call 💸
With rate limit    → blocked after 3 failed attempts

3. Order Endpoints — Inventory Manipulation
Scenario: Someone tries to block stock during a sale
Sneaky user during Big Billion Day sale:
POST /api/orders/place → iPhone 15  (books last 5 in stock)
POST /api/orders/place → iPhone 15  (books more)
POST /api/orders/place → iPhone 15  (books more)
... then cancels all orders after sale ends

Without rate limit → can manipulate your entire inventory
With rate limit    → max 10 orders per minute per user

4. Search & Product Listing — Scraping
Scenario: Competitor scrapes your entire product catalog + prices
Competitor bot:
GET /api/products/search?q=shoes    → 200 ✅
GET /api/products/search?q=shirts   → 200 ✅
GET /api/products/search?q=watches  → 200 ✅
... 10,000 requests in 1 hour

Without rate limit → your entire catalog + pricing stolen
                     your server slows down for real users
With rate limit    → blocked after 30 requests/minute per IP

5. OTP Endpoints — SMS Cost Abuse
Scenario: Someone uses your OTP to send unlimited SMS
Abuser:
POST /api/auth/send-otp → { phone: "9999999999" } → SMS sent 💸
POST /api/auth/send-otp → { phone: "9999999999" } → SMS sent 💸
POST /api/auth/send-otp → { phone: "9999999999" } → SMS sent 💸
... 500 times

Without rate limit → you pay for 500 SMS (Twilio/MSG91 charges per SMS)
With rate limit    → max 3 OTPs per 10 minutes per phone number

6. Review Endpoints — Fake Reviews
Scenario: Competitor posts fake bad reviews on your products
Competitor bot:
POST /api/products/123/review → ⭐ "Worst product ever"
POST /api/products/123/review → ⭐ "Don't buy this"
POST /api/products/123/review → ⭐ "Total waste of money"
... 100 reviews in 1 hour from same account

Without rate limit → product rating destroyed
With rate limit    → max 5 reviews per hour per user

Summary in One Table
Endpoint          Who to limit by    Limit              Why
─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/auth/login       IP                 5 / minute         Brute force
/auth/send-otp    Phone number       3 / 10 minutes     SMS cost
/payments/*       User + IP          3 / minute         Fraud
/orders/place     UserId             10 / minute        Inventory abuse
/products/search  IP                 30 / minute        Scraping
/reviews          UserId             5 / hour           Fake reviews



